# Environment for netbird-split.service (netbird-split).
#
# This file belongs to the split-tunnel fork. Upstream netbird.service never
# reads it. The unit sets NB_STATE_DIR and NB_RUNTIME_DIR to split-owned paths;
# do not override those here.
#
# Log level for the daemon:
#NB_LOG_LEVEL=info
#
# Management server for a self-hosted deployment:
#NB_MANAGEMENT_URL=https://netbird.example.com
#
# Additional daemon flags. Keep the unit's --daemon-addr and --log-file values.
#FLAGS=""
#
# The overlay interface is selected by `netbird-split up`, not by the service.
# Use a distinct name when an upstream NetBird client also runs on the host:
#   sudo netbird-split up --interface-name nbs0
